### 5. SECURITY & ACCESS CONTROLS

Licensee shall implement and maintain **industry-standard security measures** including:

```yaml
security_requirements:
  authentication:
    multi_factor: Required (TOTP, FIDO2, or equivalent)
    password_policy: 
      minimum_length: 12
      complexity: [uppercase, lowercase, numbers, special characters]
      expiry: 90 days
      history: 24 passwords
    session:
      timeout: 15 minutes of inactivity
      concurrent_sessions: 1 per user
      ip_restriction: Required for production
    rate_limiting:
      max_attempts: 5
      lockout_duration: 30 minutes
  
  encryption:
    data_at_rest: AES-256-GCM minimum
    data_in_transit: TLS 1.3 minimum
    key_management: HSM-backed or equivalent
    key_rotation: Minimum every 90 days
    database_encryption: Required
    backup_encryption: Required
  
  logging:
    audit_logging: Required for all access and operations
    log_retention: Minimum 7 years
    log_integrity: Cryptographic verification
    security_incident_reporting: Within 24 hours
    log_categories:
      - Authentication events
      - Access events
      - Verification operations
      - Configuration changes
      - Security events
      - Errors and exceptions
  
  network:
    access_restriction: Authorized IP ranges only
    remote_access: VPN required (WireGuard or IPsec)
    network_segmentation: Isolated from untrusted networks
    vulnerability_scanning: Weekly
    penetration_testing: Annual
  
  ai_security:
    model_attacks: Defenses against prompt injection, adversarial inputs
    output_sanitization: Required before displaying or storing
    data_redaction: Remove PII before model processing
```

