### 14. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

```yaml
dispute_resolution:
  negotiation:
    - Good faith negotiation: 30 days
    - Senior management involvement
    - Written correspondence required
  
  mediation:
    - If negotiation fails, mediation within 15 days
    - Mediator: Appointed by the Malaysian Mediation Centre (MMC)
    - Cost: Shared equally
    - Confidentiality: All mediation communications are without prejudice
  
  arbitration:
    - If mediation fails, final resolution by arbitration
    - Rules: Kuala Lumpur Regional Centre for Arbitration (KLRCA) Rules
    - Number of arbitrators: One
    - Language: English
    - Venue: Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia
    - Award: Final and binding on both parties
    - Enforcement: In any court of competent jurisdiction
  
  injunctive_relief:
    - Either party may seek emergency injunctive relief in court
    - Such relief is not a waiver of arbitration rights
    - Bond: Not required for injunctive relief
  
  litigation_waiver:
    - For all disputes other than emergency injunctive relief,
      the parties waive trial by jury and any right to participate
      in class actions or representative proceedings.
```

